### Changing the EC2 instance sizing using console and CLI
- We can change the instance type for example from t2.micro to t2.small when instance is in stopped state
- aws ec2 stop-instances --instance-ids <instance-id>
- aws ec2 describe-instance-attribute --instance-id <instance-id> --attribute instanceType
- aws ec2 describe-instance-types
- aws ec2 describe-instance-types --instance-types t2.micro
- aws ec2 describe-instance-types --filters Name=hibernation-supported,Values=true --query InstanceTypes[].InstanceType
- aws ec2 modify-instance-attribute --instance-id <instance-id> --instance-type "{\"Value\":\"t2.micro\"}"

### Auto scaling
- Horizontal scaling
  - scale-out: adding new instances when traffic increases
  - scale-in : removing instances when traffic reduces
- Automated capacity adjustment
- Auto scaling can be applied to
  - EC2 instances
  - Elastic contianer service (ECS)
  - Amazon DynamoDB
  - Amazon Aurora database replicas
- predictive scaling, applies to EC2 auto scaling groups. scale proactively based on historical activity patterns
